  "problem": "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix with eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=-3$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=2$ corresponding to the eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ respectively, where\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nGiven that the position of a particle at time $t$ seconds is given by the vector $x(t),$ and that $x(t)$ is the solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{\u2032}(t)=Ax(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nfind the position of the particle at $t=3$ seconds.",
